  note = {Opened: original folios 83, 85 and 91--97 (official PDF pages 84, 86 and 92--98), visually verified on 19 November 2026; folio 93 also enlarged. Folio 85 defines QSch by inverting integral radicial surjections, without identifying this with the term in cote 66. Folio 91 fixes a complete discrete valuation ring with perfect residue field and a flat finite-type source site. Folio 93 specifies finite-surjective descent on a target described, in the independently corroborated reading, as preschemes flasques compacts; no definition of flasque has yet been verified. Folio 95 explicitly calls its sheaf functor N: C(S) to C'(k) the Neron functor and gives its finite-constructible-partition formula. Folios 96--97 mark required acyclicity properties for verification, with a crossed-out justification on 96; no completed derived-functor theorem is inferred. Validated HTTP byte-range source excerpts and page images are retained, with extraction metadata in logs/A567\_cote43\_83\_85\_range\_extract.json and logs/A567\_cote43\_91\_to97\_range\_extract.json. Catalogue dating: from 1961 to approximately 1968. Michel Hua's transcription project supplied the location lead; these readings were checked against the original}
